.TH INKPAGE 1 "@INKPAGE_MAN_DATE@" "inkpage @INKPAGE_FULL_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inkpage \- simple PDF editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B inkpage
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B inkpage
edits PDF documents: annotations (inline text, images, shapes, freehand
drawing, highlighter, sticky notes), page content and pages (add, insert,
duplicate, delete, move, ruled backgrounds).
It is based on PDF4QT by Jakub Melka.
.PP
If \fIFILE\fR is given, the PDF document is opened.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR \fIpath\fR
Use the directory \fIpath\fR for the user settings, instead of
\fI~/.config/inkpage\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-drm\fR
Disable the DRM settings of the documents.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display the help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Display the version and exit.
.PP
The standard options of Qt applications are also accepted (for example
\fB\-platform\fR, \fB\-style\fR).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/inkpage/inkpage.ini
User settings (shortcuts, toolbars, styles of the annotations).
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/lidiriel/inkpage
